This repository is the design specification of cdin and uses the same license
as the cdin repository, so that text and code written against it can move
between the two without a license change.

It contains documents and one standard-library Python script (scripts/check.py).
No third-party source code is bundled. Names of third-party components that
appear in the text (SDL, Lua, libuv, Unicode, regular-expression libraries) are
references to those projects, not copies of them; each keeps its own license.
